# CUDA-variant inputs (#1013): every top-level pin from requirements.in plus
# the CUDA-only extras below. ONLY requirements-linux-amd64-cuda.txt is
# resolved from this file; the CPU and test locks never see these lines.
# Regenerate per that lock's header (deploy/aligner/README.md, "Dependency
# lock" section).
-r requirements.in
# CUDA 12 cuBLAS, solely for ctranslate2 (faster-whisper's engine). torch
# 2.15.0 is a CUDA 13.2 build and pulls cuBLAS 13 (libcublas.so.13) as
# nvidia-cublas, but ctranslate2 4.8.4 dlopens libcublas.so.12 by soname, so
# without this wheel the CUDA image has no cuBLAS ctranslate2 can load. The two
# coexist: different sonames (.12 vs .13) in different directories
# (nvidia/cublas/lib vs nvidia/cu13/lib), torch finds its own through its
# RUNPATH and the Dockerfile registers only this one with ldconfig.
# 12.8.4.1 is the exact cuBLAS ctranslate2 4.8.4's wheels were built against
# (its python/tools/prepare_build_environment_linux.sh installs
# libcublas-devel-12-8-12.8.4.1 with CUDA 12.8). Re-check that script when
# ctranslate2 moves: a CUDA 13 ctranslate2 makes this wheel unnecessary.
nvidia-cublas-cu12==12.8.4.1
